      "note": "Transthoracic echocardiogram performed 9 March 2026. Image quality is poor secondary to body habitus and limited acoustic windows; the apex and the lateral wall are not adequately visualised. Left ventricular ejection fraction estimated at 45 to 50 percent by visual assessment, though endocardial border definition is inadequate for quantitative measurement. There is a suggestion of increased wall thickness in the basal septum that cannot be characterised further on this study. Diastolic assessment is limited by the paced rhythm. Conclusion: technically limited study. Left ventricular systolic function appears mildly reduced but cannot be quantified. The question of an infiltrative process raised clinically is not answered by this study and further imaging is advised.",
